This project analyzes user behavior on social media platforms to predict engagement patterns and content preferences. It implements a pipeline that processes mock social media data, performs behavioral analysis, and builds an LSTM-based prediction model for forecasting user engagement trends. The solution demonstrates skills in deep learning, time-series forecasting, and user behavior profiling.

**Project Structure:**

1. User Credential Validation
Implemented secure credential handling using Python's getpass module
Validates platform selection (Twitter, Instagram, Facebook) and user credentials
Provides immediate feedback on validation success/failure

2. Platform-Specific Mock Data Generation
Generated synthetic user data for 3 platforms using NumPy and Pandas
Platform-specific metrics:
--Twitter: Tweets, likes, retweets, sentiment
--Instagram: Posts, likes, comments, sentiment
--Facebook: Posts, reactions, shares, sentiment
Used hashing for reproducible unique datasets based on username-platform combinations

3. Behavioral Analysis
Created composite engagement metric:
--Twitter: Likes + Retweets
--Instagram: Likes + Comments
--Facebook: Reactions + Shares
Implemented sentiment categorization (Positive/Negative/Neutral) using thresholds
Generated visualizations:
--Sentiment distribution histograms
--Engagement trend line plots
Used Seaborn and Matplotlib for professional visualizations

4. LSTM Prediction Model
Engineered time-series sequences from engagement data
Implemented data preprocessing pipeline:
--MinMax scaling (0-1 normalization)
--Sliding window sequence generation (10-step lookback)
Built LSTM neural network architecture:
--Two LSTM layers (64 and 32 units)
--Dropout regularization (20%)
--Dense output layer
Configured training with:
--Early stopping callback
--Adam optimizer
--Mean Squared Error loss
Visualized predictions vs actual engagement

5. Main Pipeline
Integrated all components into executable workflow
Implemented platform-specific analysis flows
Ensured end-to-end execution from credential validation to predictions


**Technical Highlights:**
Deep Learning: LSTM networks for time-series forecasting of engagement
User Profiling: Comprehensive behavioral metrics and sentiment analysis
Visual Analytics: Interactive Seaborn/Matplotlib visualizations
Data Engineering: Synthetic data generation with controlled variability
Modular Design: Reusable components for each processing phase


